{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"eaa3930f092a2a5511ce9d68ce1938d39e832f13c041b3b72560e0aaf0805470","slug":"host-disks","location":"/guide/host-disks.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Real hard disks","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Andrew Hutchings","given":"Andrew","family":"Hutchings"},"name":"Andrew Hutchings","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/CopperlineHQ/Copperline","keywords":["amiga","emulator","ocs","ecs","rust"],"numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/CopperlineHQ/Copperline/blob/main/docs/guide/host-disks.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/CopperlineHQ/Copperline/edit/main/docs/guide/host-disks.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"host-disks.md","url":"/docs/build/host-disks-38e3a8fb6a8297594051cc684621425d.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Copperline can give the emulated machine a real disk of this computer’s\ninstead of a hard-drive image -- any disk it can see: a card in a reader, a\nUSB drive, a drive on a SATA port. The Amiga sees the medium as it is, with\nits own Rigid Disk Block, its own partitions, its own filesystem. Nothing is\ncopied or converted, so a card taken out of an A1200 boots the same Workbench\nit booted five minutes earlier.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"MSbhEExzDN"}],"key":"OhtrskDjUt"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This writes to whole physical media rather than to a file, where a mistake\ncosts somebody their only copy of an Amiga’s system disk. The rules below are\nnot configurable.","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"eA8xxxRRlw"}],"key":"j7djAKzRQv"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"What you can attach","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"tvSUkHXBqV"}],"identifier":"what-you-can-attach","label":"What you can attach","html_id":"what-you-can-attach","implicit":true,"key":"ZnHCrwI6JH"},{"type":"code","lang":"sh","value":"copperline --list-disks","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"YDxwxUKXgy"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"names every disk, how big it is, and anything you need to know before\nchoosing one:","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"RcQQ4nwF7E"}],"key":"kc5rRtBFPW"},{"type":"code","lang":"text","value":"Host disks (name one to --host-disk, or as [[host_disk]] device):\n  sdb        Generic MassStorageClass (31.9 GB)\n  sdc        ATA Samsung SSD 870 (500.1 GB) [internal]\n  sda        ATA Ubuntu Linux-0 S (68.7 GB) [system disk, internal, mounted: /]  -- cannot be used","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"VREaBxX8Lw"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Listing reads nothing from any medium and needs no privileges, so it is safe\nto run at any time.","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"m0h2P9QHSK"}],"key":"hSXstDjBVY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every disk is offered except ","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"iTzvcEoV6K"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"the one this computer is running from","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"uQkLalWECj"}],"key":"gwpGDQARox"},{"type":"text","value":", which\nis refused by name however it is asked for -- launcher, config file, or\ncommand line. It is still listed, marked ","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"dm7iOqbFI6"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cannot be used","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"b6Sp7nNYdY"},{"type":"text","value":", because a disk\nthat silently vanished would just look like a bug. Which disk that is gets\nworked out afresh on every run from your machine’s own layout, following the\nrunning system through whatever sits under it: LVM and LUKS on Linux, an APFS\ncontainer down to the drive it is stored on for macOS. If a layout cannot be\ntraced, nothing is offered at all.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"tW2Y0fmkxa"}],"key":"yoGekIu65d"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disks on an internal bus are labelled ","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"jxmQl1yT7e"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"internal","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"BlHiR9CFIF"},{"type":"text","value":" and sorted last, but they\nare yours to use. And no RDB is ever invented over a disk that has none: an\nAmiga disk carries its own partition table, and one that does not is a disk\nCopperline will not pretend to understand.","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"F2jMybCD1G"}],"key":"nW86h8I2JP"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attaching one","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"FT9Bo2WYQG"}],"identifier":"attaching-one","label":"Attaching one","html_id":"attaching-one","implicit":true,"key":"wpkWxrJmve"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"From the launcher: ","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"key":"OXo0JTj6PQ"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Storage → Host Disk","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"key":"ghZtg5lVXl"}],"key":"x5iurzZAVb"},{"type":"text","value":", tick the disk, choose where the\nmachine should see it, and press ","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"key":"bkTwwIAqyL"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mount","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"key":"gBoS9gOTzV"}],"key":"bS3Ii3t4W7"},{"type":"text","value":". Permission is asked for there, at\nthe button you pressed, rather than later behind a machine that is starting.\nMore disks than the table shows scroll with the arrows in its top and bottom\nright corners, each greyed at its end of the list; held, they work up through\nfive speeds, a second at each.","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"key":"whKGh4J1KD"}],"key":"Ze5XDP6zBj"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"From the command line:","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"Yn7vp8PubH"}],"key":"Uk5E5GGwJZ"},{"type":"code","lang":"sh","value":"copperline --model A1200 --fast 8M KICK31.ROM --host-disk sdb\ncopperline --model A1200 --fast 8M KICK31.ROM --host-disk-read-only sdb","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"key":"IrvvWdCjRQ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Or in a configuration file:","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"ptvwhVCRZj"}],"key":"kJNBHvivyZ"},{"type":"code","lang":"toml","value":"[[host_disk]]\ndevice = \"sdb\"                 # last name shown by --list-disks\nfingerprint = \"v1-...\"         # opaque identity written by the launcher\nattach = \"ide-master\"          # ide-master (default), ide-slave, lide0-master,\n                                # lide0-slave, lide1-master, lide1-slave, or scsi0..scsi6\nread_only = true               # the default; false explicitly allows writes","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"key":"UwehPL14Sv"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lide0-*","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"lHiAMJjMLC"},{"type":"text","value":" and ","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"ZF3jHHdYFn"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lide1-*","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"lSbhBQVjh2"},{"type":"text","value":" are the two channels of a ","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"AsJGPX6A4Y"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[lide]","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"ccLNRhLYrb"},{"type":"text","value":" Zorro II IDE board\n(RIPPLE, RIDE, or AT-Bus 2008). ","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"Ebbsk7aOgS"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lide1-*","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"uzRQOdal4Y"},{"type":"text","value":" only applies to the RIPPLE\npersonality, which has two channels; RIDE and AT-Bus 2008 have only channel 0.","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"r6J1VLtEf0"}],"key":"AQ6xoGrtoN"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"device","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"tLvxQVMvsj"},{"type":"text","value":" is the host’s current enumeration name, exactly as ","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"y9k1nIoln6"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--list-disks","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"epKCU5EZ6T"},{"type":"text","value":"\nprints it: ","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"heMXNMd8SD"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sdb","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"yYsLLUYPDt"},{"type":"text","value":" on Linux, ","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"Mi4nK5kUDv"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disk4","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"q5ZL9pAZAB"},{"type":"text","value":" on macOS, or ","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"JeQORokhM8"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PhysicalDrive1","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"ZClsvTGUnF"},{"type":"text","value":" on Windows.\nThose names can change when disks are attached in a different order. The\nlauncher therefore saves ","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"SAHtMpE51I"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fingerprint","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"OvEGBqUwom"},{"type":"text","value":", an opaque identity made from the\ndisk’s reported serial/model and geometry. On the next run the fingerprint is\nauthoritative: Copperline follows the same disk to a changed name only when\nexactly one attached disk matches it, and refuses a missing or ambiguous\nmatch rather than guessing. Keep the value the launcher wrote; do not invent\nor copy one between disks.","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"tafvFfi2Bz"}],"key":"Pw1FzWed7c"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Older and hand-written entries may omit ","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"key":"vLepfdrIcf"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fingerprint","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"key":"iaJySkbcEY"},{"type":"text","value":"; they use an exact\n","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"key":"LSfzTZMdZj"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"device","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"key":"X2NUpchXdR"},{"type":"text","value":" lookup and cannot follow a renamed disk. To add one, select and mount\nthe disk afresh in the launcher, then save or launch; merely opening and\nsaving the old entry deliberately preserves the missing fingerprint. A disk\nthat cannot be resolved leaves that drive slot empty and the machine starts\nanyway, as a real Amiga does with an absent drive.","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"key":"qsOQuLoVpJ"}],"key":"pH5ZmSQStU"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":95,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persisted permission to write is deliberately narrower than fingerprint\nmatching. Removable media is always treated as weak, even if its USB bridge\nreports a serial: that value often identifies the reader rather than the card\ninside it. The same is true of any fixed disk without a credible serial or\nWWN. A fingerprint can still resolve either kind for read-only use, but select\nand mount the physical disk afresh in the launcher before every writable\nsession. Only a fixed, non-removable disk with a credible serial/WWN may reopen\nwritable from persisted configuration.","position":{"start":{"line":95,"column":1},"end":{"line":95,"column":1}},"key":"J2qFNN7lQr"}],"key":"ha3IzRfUgB"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":108,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Omitting ","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"tskP6xWIe2"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"read_only","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"n0KB3eVAku"},{"type":"text","value":" is safe: it now means read-only. This intentionally makes\nolder configs that omitted the key read-only too; set ","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"majeuKjzVO"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"read_only = false","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"altzPn3zg1"},{"type":"text","value":"\nonly after checking the selected disk. The command-line flags describe a\nchoice made for this run, so ","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"nSxZIynOce"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--host-disk","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"YbU4FO7s8h"},{"type":"text","value":" is explicitly read-write and\n","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"FJ3Z3k8hiH"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--host-disk-read-only","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"Jn41OaXFrG"},{"type":"text","value":" is protected.","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"O2NjhHvFv1"}],"key":"s34BzTWznA"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":110,"column":1},"end":{"line":110,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read-only first","position":{"start":{"line":110,"column":1},"end":{"line":110,"column":1}},"key":"FXp8p2K9C9"}],"identifier":"read-only-first","label":"Read-only first","html_id":"read-only-first","implicit":true,"key":"vVFsXxp8TW"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":112,"column":1},"end":{"line":113,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attach a disk read-only the first time. It costs one boot and tells you more\nthan anything else:","position":{"start":{"line":112,"column":1},"end":{"line":112,"column":1}},"key":"NzUPvfGLl5"}],"key":"jdr47toxus"},{"type":"code","lang":"sh","value":"copperline --model A1200 --fast 8M KICK31.ROM --host-disk-read-only sdb","position":{"start":{"line":115,"column":1},"end":{"line":117,"column":1}},"key":"LpdE1uIWBO"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":121,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"An Amiga filesystem writes when it mounts -- PFS marks the volume in use --\nso a ","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":119,"column":1}},"key":"jEUXigvGxb"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":119,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"correct","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":119,"column":1}},"key":"pcsHfGpiU9"}],"key":"GDp1Lhf9GW"},{"type":"text","value":" read-only attach boots far enough to raise the guest’s own\nwrite error, and the log names the same block:","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":119,"column":1}},"key":"fazULtZqvm"}],"key":"XzzvDGNMCw"},{"type":"code","lang":"text","value":"blockdev: sdb is attached read-only, so the guest's write to sector 1026146\n          was refused; tick R/W (or set `read_only = false`) to let it write","position":{"start":{"line":123,"column":1},"end":{"line":126,"column":1}},"key":"cxLQjyN7Ac"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":128,"column":1},"end":{"line":129,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"That proves the read path end to end. Attach it read-write and it should\nreach Workbench with no requester at all.","position":{"start":{"line":128,"column":1},"end":{"line":128,"column":1}},"key":"k6IoZCAqBR"}],"key":"ha0UDSAsHL"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":131,"column":1},"end":{"line":131,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"While the machine has it","position":{"start":{"line":131,"column":1},"end":{"line":131,"column":1}},"key":"IPv2wiXMqh"}],"identifier":"while-the-machine-has-it","label":"While the machine has it","html_id":"while-the-machine-has-it","implicit":true,"key":"ycdhdX9cr9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":133,"column":1},"end":{"line":138,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The disk is taken from the host completely. Volumes mounted from it are\nunmounted first -- the host writing its own metadata under a guest that\ncannot account for it changing is a hazard either way -- and the medium stays\nthe machine’s until you give it back. If something else still has a file open\non the disk, the attach fails and says so rather than taking it out from\nunderneath.","position":{"start":{"line":133,"column":1},"end":{"line":133,"column":1}},"key":"uIOxCw2M6V"}],"key":"UG5yEp8aui"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":140,"column":1},"end":{"line":144,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is taken once, at ","position":{"start":{"line":140,"column":1},"end":{"line":140,"column":1}},"key":"nUnpGIP9j1"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":140,"column":1},"end":{"line":140,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mount","position":{"start":{"line":140,"column":1},"end":{"line":140,"column":1}},"key":"ecdbqPAgt5"}],"key":"D9weTfkVxu"},{"type":"text","value":" (or when a configuration-driven run first\nstarts), and stays taken for the 